AgriME – Agri Made Easy
Project Overview, Requirements and User Roles

1. Project Overview
Project Title: AgriME – Agri Made Easy
Project Type: AI-Powered Smart Agriculture Platform
1.1 Introduction
AgriME is an intelligent agricultural platform designed to help farmers make better decisions related to crop selling, agricultural product purchasing, farm machinery, and government schemes.
The platform brings important agricultural services together in a single system. Farmers can view current crop prices, compare prices across different markets, get AI-based crop price predictions, purchase agricultural products, find nearby dealers, book farm machinery, and discover government schemes relevant to their farming activities.
1.2 Problem
Farmers often have to depend on different sources to obtain agricultural information and services. They may not easily know:
    • The current price of their crop in different markets.
    • Which nearby market offers a better price.
    • Whether the crop price may increase or decrease in the near future.
    • Where to purchase fertilizers, pesticides, seeds, and other agricultural products.
    • Where nearby agricultural dealers are located and how to contact them.
    • Where to find and book tractors, paddy harvesters, and other farm machinery.
    • Which government agricultural schemes they may be eligible for.
AgriME aims to bring these requirements together into one farmer-friendly platform.
1.3 Proposed Solution
AgriME provides a centralized platform where farmers can access agricultural market information and services based on their location and farming requirements.
The platform will initially focus on five major areas:
    1. Real-Time Crop Price Comparison
    2. AI-Based Crop Price Prediction
    3. Agricultural E-Commerce
    4. Agricultural Government Scheme Recommendation
    5. Farm Machinery Booking
Additional supporting features include farmer profiles, dealer information, location-based services, and market comparison.
1.4 Target Users
The primary target users are farmers, particularly small and medium-scale farmers who need easy access to agricultural market information and services.
Other users include:
    • Agricultural product dealers and sellers
    • Farm machinery owners/service providers
    • Platform administrators

2. System Requirements
2.1 Functional Requirements
FR-01 – Farmer Registration and Profile
The system shall allow farmers to create an account and provide basic information such as:
    • Name
    • Contact information
    • Location
    • Crops cultivated
    • Farm-related information
The farmer profile will be used to provide personalized services.
FR-02 – Seasonal Crop Price Display
The system shall display current prices of important seasonal crops on the Home page.
For example, depending on season and location, crops such as:
    • Paddy
    • Groundnut
may be highlighted on the dashboard.
FR-03 – Crop Price Comparison
The system shall allow farmers to view and compare crop prices from different agricultural markets.
The farmer shall be able to filter markets based on distance, such as:
    • Within 25 km
    • Within 50 km
    • Within 100 km
    • More than 100 km
    • All locations
The system shall also provide sorting options such as highest price, nearest market, and recently updated price.
FR-04 – Crop Price Prediction
The system shall provide AI/ML-based predictions of future crop prices.
The prediction module shall provide information such as:
    • Current price
    • Predicted price range
    • Price trend
    • Historical price information
    • Prediction period
The prediction shall be presented as an estimate and not as a guaranteed future price.
FR-05 – Agricultural E-Commerce
The system shall allow farmers to browse and purchase agricultural products such as:
    • Seeds
    • Fertilizers
    • Pesticides
    • Agricultural equipment
Products shall contain relevant information such as price, seller/dealer, availability, and product details.
FR-06 – Dealer Information
The system shall provide information about nearby agricultural dealers.
Dealer information may include:
    • Dealer name
    • Location
    • Distance
    • Contact details
    • Products/services available
    • Operating information
Farmers shall be able to locate and contact dealers.
FR-07 – Farm Machinery Booking
The system shall allow farmers to search and book agricultural machinery such as:
    • Tractors
    • Paddy harvesters
    • Rotavators
    • Other farm equipment
The system shall display:
    • Machinery details
    • Owner/service provider
    • Location
    • Rental price
    • Availability
    • Booking date and time
The system shall prevent conflicting bookings for the same machinery.
FR-08 – Government Scheme Recommendation
The system shall recommend relevant agricultural government schemes based on farmer information such as:
    • Location
    • Crop
    • Land-related information
    • Farming requirements
    • Other eligibility information
The system shall provide scheme details such as benefits, eligibility requirements, required documents, and official application information where available.
FR-09 – Location-Based Services
The system shall use the farmer's selected location to provide relevant:
    • Market information
    • Crop prices
    • Dealers
    • Machinery
    • Agricultural services
FR-10 – Administrator Management
The administrator shall be able to manage and monitor:
    • Farmers
    • Dealers
    • Products
    • Machinery listings
    • Bookings
    • Government scheme information
    • Market-related data

2.2 Non-Functional Requirements
NFR-01 – Usability
The system should provide a simple and easy-to-understand interface suitable for farmers with different levels of technical knowledge.
NFR-02 – Performance
The system should load important information such as crop prices and dashboard content quickly.
NFR-03 – Responsiveness
The website should work properly on:
    • Desktop computers
    • Tablets
    • Mobile devices
NFR-04 – Security
User accounts and personal information should be protected using appropriate authentication and authorization mechanisms.
NFR-05 – Reliability
The system should provide accurate and appropriately updated information wherever reliable data sources are available.
NFR-06 – Scalability
The system should be designed so that additional crops, markets, dealers, products, machinery, and users can be added as the platform grows.

3. User Roles
3.1 Farmer
The farmer is the primary user of AgriME.
The farmer can:
    • Create and manage a profile.
    • View seasonal crop prices.
    • Compare prices across markets.
    • Check crop price predictions.
    • Browse and purchase agricultural products.
    • Find nearby dealers.
    • Contact dealers.
    • Search for farm machinery.
    • Check machinery availability.
    • Book tractors, harvesters, and other machinery.
    • View recommended government schemes.

3.2 Agricultural Dealer / Seller
Dealers and agricultural sellers provide products and services through the platform.
They can:
    • Create and manage a dealer profile.
    • Add agricultural products.
    • Update product prices and availability.
    • Provide contact and location information.
    • Receive and manage customer orders.
    • Manage their listed services/products.

3.3 Machinery Owner / Service Provider
Machinery owners or agricultural service providers can:
    • Register their machinery.
    • Add machinery details.
    • Set rental prices.
    • Specify location.
    • Set availability.
    • View booking requests.
    • Accept or reject bookings.
    • Manage their booking schedule.

3.4 Administrator
The administrator manages the overall platform.
The administrator can:
    • Manage users.
    • Verify and manage dealers.
    • Manage product information.
    • Manage machinery listings.
    • Monitor bookings.
    • Manage government scheme information.
    • Manage agricultural market information.
    • Monitor the overall system.

				